  {
   "block": "ROM: matrix engine base lanes (196,608 on 2 dies)",
   "verdict": "RIGHT-SIZED (ROM-read bound)",
   "why": "each die's 6,144 groups are the most its half of the 8-bit ROM feeds (read headroom 1.017; 6,656 groups a die would be 0.939); the compute chain binds the autoregressive token (101,037 vs a 92,161-cycle KV floor); half the groups is 157,445 cycles (+56% a token) in the calibrated model"
  },
  {
   "block": "ROM: 4 lane copies a die",
   "verdict": "JUSTIFIED (DFlash only), conditional on power",
   "why": "idle in autoregressive decode and in KV-bound batches (each user's KV is its own); they carry the DFlash block-5 verify (2.076x single-user tokens/s). Under the 474.6 W per-die liquid limit the capped DFlash / autoregressive rates are 18,720 / 10,874 tokens/s on the production lane (scenario B: the copies pay) and 6,680 / 7,859 on the routed 3.97 pJ/MAC lane (scenario A: they do not)"
  },
  {
   "block": "ROM: weight ROM read path",
   "verdict": "RIGHT-SIZED (binding on the lane count)",
   "why": "one 8-bit weight a lane a cycle, 98,304.0 B a cycle a die at read headroom 1.017; the sweep is on the single user's chain (38,880 cycles)"
  },
  {
   "block": "ROM: vector stream unit (1,024 lanes; SFUs and reducers on its lanes)",
   "verdict": "RIGHT-SIZED",
   "why": "calibrated: 512 lanes is 104,069 cycles (+3.0% a token), 2,048 is 99,521 (-1.5%)"
