   "verdict": "RIGHT-SIZED (beachfront-limited)",
   "why": "the KV floor (92,161 cycles) sits 9% under the autoregressive chain; the stacks are what each die's free edge holds, and KV-bound batches bind on them"
  },
  {
   "block": "ROM: KV ring buffer (one a die)",
   "verdict": "JUSTIFIED (the O4 record's sizing; halving it is an open lever)",
   "why": "each die's ring holds one layer plus the package's refresh cover (19.3 MB, the O4 record's sizing); the die's own KV heads fill 50% of it, so halving it would free about 3 mm2 a die"
  },
  {
   "block": "ROM: KV ring buffer's engine read port",
   "verdict": "JUSTIFIED (latency)",
   "why": "one FP8 word a group a cycle is the engine's attention operand rate: the scores and P.V passes read a layer's KV in 512 cycles on the chain; a narrower port lengthens every layer's attention stage"
  },
  {
   "block": "ROM: UCIe link",
